      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_a2f7ebaa17f4b5167f9ad650e47860af4f78ee24d3e68b90ed049f65c9aa54d1",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Fourier space diagonalizes translation-invariant operators, so an analytic scalar function becomes a nonlocal operator through its multiplier. This definition clarifies what the symbol preserves—momentum modes—and what it depends on—flat translation symmetry and a suitable Fourier-domain class.",
