    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_238b389bdfeddf3b6330a3166741b6021fc912170834f41dcf62fe0421a542d8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Flat-space Fourier multiplication supplies a concrete definition of the nonlocal xi wave operator, but that diagonal representation is unavailable on curved spacetime and promotion to a quantum field additionally requires an operator-valued distribution, state space, vacuum, covariance, spectral measure, and positivity choices; the factorized local-mode formulas are proposed surrogates for these changes rather than automatic extensions.",
