    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_41dbd42aa5d699b88250bf7ffaec641309058bdf521ad01eb5b4837b8d0f6012",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The availability of real paired factors depends on the symmetry of the completed symbol: xi and the phase-corrected Riemann-Siegel function are real on the critical line and have conjugate zero structure, whereas completed Dirichlet L-functions for non-real characters need not have zero symmetry about the real axis, so the same proposed zero-to-mode construction would have a different pairing problem.",
