    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6a788b88042673dbeb42b0c07d4f12859643e98c5201a637eb9f5592ada42fe3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For elliptic-curve L-functions, modularity supplies an analytically continued Dirichlet series with a functional equation, while the conjectural order-r zero at s=1 is formally transported by substituting s=1+i box into a leading operator term proportional to (i box)^r; this carries an arithmetic multiplicity into an operator expansion without validating a physical interpretation.",
